--TEST--
A user attribute on an enum, an enum case or a class constant is `E0871`, and the same attribute on a class, a method and a property compiles
--FILE--
<?nvs
type Label = {text: string};

#[Label(text: "suit")]
enum Suit {
    #[Label(text: "hearts")]
    Hearts,
    Spades,
}

#[Label(text: "shop")]
class Shop {
    #[Label(text: "limit")]
    public const int LIMIT = 3;

    #[Label(text: "name")]
    public string $name = "";

    #[Label(text: "open")]
    public function open(): void {}
}

echo Shop::LIMIT, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0871]: an attribute cannot be written on an enum
%A
error[E0871]: an attribute cannot be written on an enum case
%A
error[E0871]: an attribute cannot be written on a class constant
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
